> A zero-weight RBM is uniform over visible states

With all biases and weights zero, each of the256 visible states has probability1/256. Summing out four hidden bits gives free energy minus4log2; logZ is12log2. Their sum is8log2.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/restricted_boltzmann_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");n::ParameterStore p(1);m::RbmParameters(p,8,4);for(auto& key:p.names())p.set(key,n::zeros_like(p.at(key)));auto z=m::RbmLogPartition(p,8);auto values=n::stack({m::RbmFreeEnergy(p,n::zeros({1,8})).reshape({}),z,m::RbmFreeEnergy(p,n::zeros({1,8})).reshape({})+z},0);if(std::abs(values.to_vector<float>()[2]-8*std::log(2.))>1e-6)return 1;
std::print("| coordinate | computed value |\n|---:|---:|\n");auto v=values.to_vector<double>();for(size_t i=0;i<v.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n",i,v[i]);n::save_npz("build/restricted_boltzmann_worked.npz",{{"values",values}});dm::graphics::RPlot::create().bars(n::arange(0,std::int64_t(v.size())).to_vector<double>(),v,"native values",{37,99,235}).title("A zero-weight RBM is uniform over visible states").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/restricted_boltzmann_worked.svg");}
```
